octoshield (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add editable Conference, Public, Office and Home profiles, custom copies,
    global switching, individual control overrides and explicit restoration.
  * Show verified live protection status, profile mismatches and unavailable
    observations through shared native desktop and Whiptail interfaces.
  * Manage scoped IPv4/IPv6 firewall exceptions with kernel-enforced UTC
    expiry; prevent temporary grants reopening from disk after reboot, retain
    outgoing access and switch active policies without resetting UFW.
  * Scope USB approvals to the effective profile, reevaluate attached devices,
    expire temporary trust on switching and provide explicit trust revocation.
  * Inspect container exposure, Thunderbolt/USB4, Secure Boot and encryption;
    notify unlocked sessions of blocked devices and network changes.
  * Add explicit official-release checks and in-place Debian upgrades that
    preserve policies, profiles, user preferences and recovery snapshots.
  * Start the status observer without selecting a protection profile; verify
    genuine upgrades from published 1.0.0 packages in the Ubuntu CI matrix.

 -- OctoLeo <octoleo@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:29:45 +0000

octoshield (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release the native GNOME application and Whiptail command-line interface
    with shared firewall, USB authorization, network, service, sudo, security
    update, AppArmor, and desktop protection controls.
  * Require reviewed changes and administrator authorization for system actions;
    retain private configuration recovery records and optional event monitoring.
  * Provide Ubuntu 24.04 and 26.04 Debian packages, system light/dark appearance,
    application metadata, release screenshots, and optional signed APT updates.
  * Preserve administrator-selected protections during package upgrades and
    removal; installing OctoShield does not automatically enable hardening.

 -- OctoLeo <octoleo@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:32:57 +0000

octoshield (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add native GNOME desktop controls alongside the existing terminal interface.
  * Package the application, least-privilege helper, desktop integration, and
    optional monitoring without enabling hardening during package installation.

